    [Performance][0.32.0] Optimize KDA RecoverSSM aligned state commit (#20524)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Cherry-pick #20474 onto `releases/v0.32.0rc`: optimize GLM KDA
    RecoverSSM aligned state commit with separate boundary/non-boundary
    routing and A5 grouped-head support. Include the serving-documentation
    cleanup.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Lower commit latency without new serving options or cache-layout
    changes. Small or boundary-heavy workloads can regress; see the
    referenced measurements.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    Validated this head with **vLLM v0.32.0**
    (`5df63a7203cdb9328d824a27b682e77c7b9928be`). A3/A5 each passed 212
    tests and 1,552 independent FP64 operator-output comparisons, plus 60
    same-runtime operator A/B cases.
    
    Whole-model ReplaySSM OFF/ON comparisons use prefix caching, target/MTP
    graphs and true C90 decode. Each arm includes full 1,319-question GSM8K
    evaluation; all 48 CPU/NPU traces were checked. [Detailed results,
    acceptance, accuracy deltas, regressions and compilation
    audit](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/pull/20524#issuecomment-6554091747).
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/544f182d9f0c9bfe8bd7645525951d5e3692a542
    
    ---------
    
    Signed-off-by: drslark <slarksblood@qq.com>
